# TBC Corporation (NTW) certificate chain -- the pieces their gateways do not send.
#
# Both TBC hosts serve ONLY their leaf certificate and omit the intermediate, so a normal
# verification fails with "unable to get local issuer certificate". Browsers hide this by
# fetching the intermediate from the certificate's AIA extension; requests does not.
#
# Each file below was fetched from the exact URL named in the AIA extension of the certificate
# it signs, and verified with `openssl verify` against the real leaf before being committed:
#
#   tbcservicesqa.tbccorp.com (QA)   leaf -> "Go Daddy Secure Certificate Authority - G2"
#                                         -> "Go Daddy Root Certificate Authority - G2"  [in certifi]
#   services.tbccorp.com (production) leaf -> "GoDaddy TLS Intermediate CA DV - R1v1"
#                                         -> "GoDaddy TLS Root CA - R1"                  [NOT in certifi]
#
# That last line is why the root is here too: it was issued 2025-08-28 and has not reached the
# Mozilla set certifi ships, so production cannot be verified without it. It is trusted ONLY by
# this client (see api_client._verify), never added to the system store.
#
# These are long-lived (2031, 2040) but not permanent. If TBC's gateway starts failing TLS,
# re-read the AIA URLs from their current leaf rather than disabling verification.

